.TH poi-tracker 1 2026-08-12 "sandogasa 0.19.4" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
poi\-tracker \- Package\-of\-interest tracker for Fedora, EPEL, and CentOS SIGs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpoi\-tracker\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Package\-of\-interest tracker for Fedora, EPEL, and CentOS SIGs
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<INVENTORY>\fR
Path(s) to inventory TOML file(s)
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to scan for *.toml inventory files
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS poi-tracker add
\fBpoi\-tracker add\fR [\fB\-\-poc\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-team\fR] [\fB\-\-task\fR] [\fB\-\-rpm\fR] [\fB\-\-workload\fR] [\fB\-\-track\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.PP
Add a package to the inventory
.TP
\fB\-\-poc\fR \fI<POC>\fR
Point of contact ("Name <email>")
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Reason for tracking
.TP
\fB\-\-team\fR \fI<TEAM>\fR
Team responsible
.TP
\fB\-\-task\fR \fI<TASK>\fR
Internal task/ticket reference
.TP
\fB\-\-rpm\fR \fI<RPM>\fR
Binary RPM subpackage(s) to track (comma\-separated or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-workload\fR \fI<WORKLOAD>\fR
Workload tag(s) (comma\-separated or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-track\fR \fI<TRACK>\fR
Track branch for hs\-relmon (e.g. upstream, fedora\-rawhide)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Source RPM name
.SS poi-tracker adopt
\fBpoi\-tracker adopt\fR [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Adopt orphaned inventory packages on dist\-git
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-token\fR \fI<API_TOKEN>\fR
Dist\-git API token with the `modify_project` ACL (or set PAGURE_API_TOKEN, or run `poi\-tracker config`)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPAGURE_API_TOKEN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview orphaned packages without adopting them
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Adopt every orphaned match without per\-package prompts
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker config
\fBpoi\-tracker config\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Configure poi\-tracker (Bugzilla API key, etc.)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker export
\fBpoi\-tracker export\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.PP
Export inventory to another format
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker export content-resolver
\fBpoi\-tracker export content\-resolver\fR [\fB\-\-workload\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Export as content\-resolver YAML
.TP
\fB\-\-workload\fR \fI<WORKLOAD>\fR
Export only this workload
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output file (default: {workload\-name}.yaml)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker export hs-relmon
\fBpoi\-tracker export hs\-relmon\fR [\fB\-\-workload\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-distros\fR] [\fB\-\-track\fR] [\fB\-\-prune\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Export as hs\-relmon manifest TOML
.TP
\fB\-\-workload\fR \fI<WORKLOAD>\fR
Filter by workload
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output file (default: stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-distros\fR \fI<DISTROS>\fR [default: upstream,fedora,centos,hyperscale]
Default distros list
.TP
\fB\-\-track\fR \fI<TRACK>\fR [default: upstream]
Default tracking branch
.TP
\fB\-\-prune\fR
Remove manifest entries not in the inventory
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker find
\fBpoi\-tracker find\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.PP
Find which inventory file(s) contain a package
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Source RPM name to search for
.SS poi-tracker import
\fBpoi\-tracker import\fR [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-private\-fields\fR] [\fB\-\-workload\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIJSON_FILE\fR> 
.PP
Import from legacy JSON format
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: inventory.toml]
Output path for TOML inventory
.TP
\fB\-\-private\-fields\fR \fI<FIELD,...>\fR
Fields to mark as private (stripped on export)
.TP
\fB\-\-workload\fR \fI<WORKLOAD,...>\fR
Workload tag(s) to apply to all imported packages
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIJSON_FILE\fR>
Path to legacy JSON inventory file
.SS poi-tracker prune-retired
\fBpoi\-tracker prune\-retired\fR [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Mark (or remove) packages no longer carried on any active branch (dist\-git project gone or retired everywhere)
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH,...>\fR
Active branch(es) to check against (CSV or repeated; e.g. `rawhide,f44,epel9`). Default: queried from Bodhi\*(Aqs active releases, plus rawhide
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<JOBS>\fR [default: 8]
Parallel dist\-git queries
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview without modifying the inventory
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\fR
Delete matched packages from the inventory instead of marking them `unshipped` (the default; marking survives re\-syncs and lets triage\-retired keep closing bugs)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker remove
\fBpoi\-tracker remove\fR [\fB\-\-rpm\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.PP
Remove a package from the inventory
.TP
\fB\-\-rpm\fR \fI<RPM>\fR
Remove specific binary RPM(s) instead of the whole package
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Source RPM name to remove
.SS poi-tracker semver-audit
\fBpoi\-tracker semver\-audit\fR [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-\-batch\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-breaking\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Audit pending upstream updates by semver impact, flagging which are non\-breaking, breaking, or need review
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-\-batch\fR [\fI<EMAIL>\fR]
Batch mode: one Bugzilla query for bugs assigned to or CC\*(Aqing EMAIL (default: the configured email), matched against the inventory locally. Much faster on a large inventory, but misses bugs where EMAIL is neither assignee nor CC\*(Aqd
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-breaking\fR
Show only non\-breaking updates
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker show
\fBpoi\-tracker show\fR [\fB\-\-workload\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Show inventory contents
.TP
\fB\-\-workload\fR \fI<WORKLOAD>\fR
Filter by workload
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON instead of human\-readable
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker sync-distgit
\fBpoi\-tracker sync\-distgit\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-fast\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-groups\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\fR] [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-auto\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-\-prune\fR] [\fB\-\-mark\-unshipped\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-\-per\-page\fR] [\fB\-\-workload\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Sync inventory from Fedora dist\-git (Pagure) access
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
Import packages for this dist\-git user
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
Import packages for this dist\-git group
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: inventory.toml]
Output TOML file
.TP
\fB\-\-fast\fR
One owner\-alias request instead of a prefix scan. Direct owner/admin/commit only: collaborator/ticket grants are missed (and removed under \-\-prune). Implies \-\-no\-groups
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-groups\fR
Exclude group\-only access
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-group\fR \fI<GROUP,...>\fR
Keep only these groups (CSV or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-group\fR \fI<GROUP,...>\fR
Drop these groups (CSV or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Exclude packages by glob (CSV or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<PATTERN>\fR
Name pattern for a single patterned query
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-pattern\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
Start the prefix scan at this prefix
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-pattern\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
Stop the prefix scan before this prefix
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-prefix\fR
Query by a\-z/0\-9 prefix (\-\-user default)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-auto\-prefix\fR
Single query; may 504 for a \-\-user sync
.TP
\fB\-\-prune\fR
Remove packages no longer in dist\-git results
.TP
\fB\-\-mark\-unshipped\fR
Mark packages added by this sync that are already retired everywhere (like prune\-retired)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<JOBS>\fR [default: 8]
Parallel dist\-git queries for \-\-mark\-unshipped
.TP
\fB\-\-per\-page\fR \fI<PER_PAGE>\fR [default: 100]
Pagure API page size
.TP
\fB\-\-workload\fR \fI<WORKLOAD,...>\fR
Workload tags (CSV or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Inventory name (default: user/group)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker sync-gitlab
\fBpoi\-tracker sync\-gitlab\fR [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-preset\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\fR] [\fB\-\-prune\fR] [\fB\-\-workload\fR] [\fB\-\-mark\-unshipped\fR] [\fB\-\-centos\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Sync inventory from a GitLab RPM group
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
GitLab group URL
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fI<PRESET>\fR
Preset: hyperscale, proposed\-updates, centos\-stream
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: inventory.toml]
Output TOML file
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Exclude packages by glob (CSV or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-prune\fR
Remove packages no longer in GitLab results
.TP
\fB\-\-workload\fR \fI<WORKLOAD,...>\fR
Workload tags (CSV or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-mark\-unshipped\fR
Mark archived projects with no released CBS build as unshipped (Hyperscale: RHEL or Stream; Proposed Updates: Stream only)
.TP
\fB\-\-centos\-release\fR \fI<REL,...>\fR [default: 9,10]
CentOS releases to count as currently shipped (CSV)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Inventory name (default: derived from group)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker triage-retired
\fBpoi\-tracker triage\-retired\fR [\fB\-\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-\-batch\fR] [\fB\-\-all\-reporters\fR] [\fB\-\-mark\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-claim\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Close open release\-monitoring bugs as CANTFIX for any inventoried package that is retired on a dist\-git branch
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH,...>\fR [default: rawhide]
Dist\-git branch(es) to check retirement against (CSV or repeated; e.g. `rawhide`, `epel10`, `f43`). Each branch scopes its own Bugzilla search — a `rawhide` retirement closes the Fedora/rawhide bug, an `epel9` retirement closes the Fedora EPEL/epel9 bug. A package retired on one branch but live on another only has bugs closed where it\*(Aqs dead
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-\-batch\fR [\fI<EMAIL>\fR]
Batch mode: one Bugzilla query for bugs assigned to or CC\*(Aqing EMAIL (default: the configured email), matched against the inventory locally. Much faster on a large inventory, but misses bugs where EMAIL is neither assignee nor CC\*(Aqd
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-reporters\fR
Close ALL open bugs on retired branches, not just release\-monitoring (Anitya) bugs. Use with care: this closes human\-filed bugs (CVEs, FTBFS, etc.) too
.TP
\fB\-\-mark\fR
Record results in the inventory\*(Aqs `retired_on` markers (adds and removes; needs a single \-i file)
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\fR \fI<API_KEY>\fR
Bugzilla API key (or set BUGZILLA_API_KEY env var, or run `poi\-tracker config`)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBBUGZILLA_API_KEY\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-claim\fR
Also set `assigned_to` on each closed bug to the Bugzilla email set via `poi\-tracker config`. Interactive mode prompts; with `\-y` this flag is the only way to claim
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview closures without applying them
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker triage-updates
\fBpoi\-tracker triage\-updates\fR [\fB\-\-pattern\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-end\-with\fR] [\fB\-\-batch\fR] [\fB\-\-close\-stale\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-stale\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-claim\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Triage open release\-monitoring bugs for inventoried packages by bumping their Bugzilla priority to match the inventory
.TP
\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fI<GLOB,...>\fR
Only process packages matching this glob (e.g. `rust\-*`; a bare name matches exactly). Comma\-separated or repeated; default: all packages
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume from this package onwards (inclusive), in the inventory\*(Aqs iteration order
.TP
\fB\-\-end\-with\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Stop after this package (inclusive). Combine with `\-\-start\-from` to bound a sub\-range
.TP
\fB\-\-batch\fR [\fI<EMAIL>\fR]
Batch mode: one Bugzilla query for bugs assigned to or CC\*(Aqing EMAIL (default: the configured email), matched against the inventory locally. Much faster on a large inventory, but misses bugs where EMAIL is neither assignee nor CC\*(Aqd
.TP
\fB\-\-close\-stale\fR
Close partially\-addressed bugs without asking
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-stale\fR
Skip the Bodhi check for already\-built updates
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\fR \fI<API_KEY>\fR
Bugzilla API key (or set BUGZILLA_API_KEY env var, or run `poi\-tracker config`)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBBUGZILLA_API_KEY\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-claim\fR
Also set `assigned_to` on each closed bug to the Bugzilla email set via `poi\-tracker config`. Interactive mode prompts; with `\-y` this flag is the only way to claim
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview updates without applying them
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS poi-tracker validate
\fBpoi\-tracker validate\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Validate inventory consistency
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
